---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { CACHE_SOURCE, cacheScenarios } from '../data/cache-explorer';
import '../styles/cache-explorer.css';
---

<Layout title="Cache explorer · Gufo" description="An interactive guide to Gufo’s proposed hybrid cache: live sessions, exact checkpoints, shared KV provenance, memory budgets and durable disk restores.">
  <Navbar currentPath="/cache" />
  <main class="cache-page">
    <div class="cache-breadcrumb"><a href="/docs#serving">Documentation</a><span>/</span><span>Cache explorer</span></div>
    <header class="cache-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="cache-eyebrow"><span class="cache-status-dot"></span> Explore the proposed hybrid cache</p>
        <h1>Compute a prefix once.<br /><span>Remember where you left off.</span></h1>
        <p class="cache-intro">Follow conversations through Gufo’s cache. Move through user turns, tool results and session changes to see what is reused, what is copied, and how checkpoints serve different execution slots.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="cache-source" href={`${CACHE_SOURCE}/README.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Based on the cache redesign<br /><b>Research revision 5e401f9b ↗</b></a>
    </header>

    <div class="cache-concepts">
      <article><span class="concept-symbol session-symbol">01</span><div><h2>Session</h2><p>Mutable execution state. Its live frontier includes prompt and generated tokens.</p></div></article>
      <article><span class="concept-symbol checkpoint-symbol">02</span><div><h2>Checkpoint</h2><p>Frozen state at an exact token boundary. Recurrent state cannot simply be trimmed.</p></div></article>
      <article><span class="concept-symbol chunk-symbol">03</span><div><h2>Shared chunk</h2><p>In the proposal, 2,048 KV rows retained once by checkpoints with common provenance.</p></div></article>
    </div>

    <section class="cache-lab" aria-labelledby="walkthrough-heading">
      <div class="cache-section-heading"><div><p class="cache-eyebrow">01 / Walk through the state</p><h2 id="walkthrough-heading">Choose a cache story</h2></div><label class="cache-model-label">Model<select id="cache-model"><option value="flash" selected>Flash-Next · MTP</option><option value="qwen">27B · DFlash2</option></select></label></div>
      <div class="cache-scenarios" aria-label="Cache scenarios">
        {cacheScenarios.map((s, i) => <button type="button" class={`scenario-button ${i === 0 ? 'active' : ''}`} data-scenario={s.id} aria-pressed={i === 0}><span>{s.name}</span><small>{s.caption}</small></button>)}
      </div>
      <div class="cache-tree-panel">
        <div class="cache-tree-header">
          <div><p class="cache-eyebrow">Conversation tree</p><p id="cache-conversation-context" class="cache-tree-context"></p></div>
          <div class="cache-playback"><button type="button" id="cache-prev" aria-label="Previous step">←</button><button type="button" id="cache-play">Play story</button><button type="button" id="cache-next" aria-label="Next step">→</button><span id="cache-step-number" class="cache-step-number">Step 1</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="cache-tree-body">
          <ol id="cache-tree-lanes" class="cache-tree-lanes" aria-label="Conversation branches"></ol>
          <div id="cache-tree-scroll" class="cache-tree-scroll"><div id="cache-tree" class="cache-tree" role="toolbar" aria-label="Conversation turns. Use the arrow keys to move through time."></div></div>
        </div>
        <div class="cache-tree-footer">
          <p id="cache-tree-readout" class="cache-tree-readout"></p>
          <div class="cache-tree-legend"><span><i class="node-user"></i>User</span><span><i class="node-assistant"></i>Gufo</span><span><i class="node-tool"></i>Tool result</span><span><i class="node-event"></i>Cache event</span><span><i class="node-history"></i>History of the selected turn</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p id="cache-step-status" class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
      <div class="cache-key">
        <div class="cache-key-group"><span class="cache-key-title">Cache state</span><span><i class="legend-reused"></i>Reused prefix</span><span><i class="legend-new"></i>Needs prefill</span><span><i class="legend-fixed"></i>Fixed state</span><span><i class="legend-queued"></i>Queued for disk</span><span><i class="legend-durable"></i>Durable on disk</span></div>
        <div class="cache-key-group"><label class="cache-diff-switch"><input id="cache-diff-toggle" type="checkbox" role="switch" checked autocomplete="off" />Highlight changes</label><span><i class="key-added"></i>+ New in this step</span><span><i class="key-changed"></i>~ Changed</span><span><i class="key-removed"></i>− Removed · marked on the earlier card</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cache-carousel" id="cache-state">
        <div id="cache-diff" class="cache-diff" aria-label="Changes from the earlier state"></div>
        <div id="cache-peek-prev" class="cache-peek cache-peek-prev" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <article id="cache-previous" class="cache-lane cache-card is-previous" aria-label="Cache state at the earlier step"></article>
        <article id="cache-hybrid" class="cache-lane hybrid-lane cache-card is-current" aria-label="Cache state at the selected turn"></article>
        <div id="cache-peek-next" class="cache-peek cache-peek-next" aria-hidden="true"></div>
        <aside class="cache-inspector" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"><span class="cache-eyebrow">State inspector</span><h3 id="cache-inspector-title"></h3><p id="cache-inspector-copy"></p></aside>
      </div>
      <p id="cache-lesson" class="cache-lesson"></p>
      <p class="cache-slot-explanation">This walkthrough uses <code>--sessions 2</code> to show slot reuse with just three conversations. Gufo supports a configurable pool of up to 8 slots. More slots keep more live histories available and use more memory. Retained checkpoints are separate: up to 128 records, subject to the cache budget.</p>
      <p class="cache-method-note">These illustrative histories explain the proposed design. Slot assignments and checkpoint sets are chosen to show each mechanism; small template suffixes are omitted. RAM totals include fixed state, private tails and unique KV rows, including reserved spill capacity for borrowed rows. Execution-slot memory is additional.</p>
      <noscript><p class="cache-noscript">Enable JavaScript to step through the visualization. The concepts and source links on this page remain available without it.</p></noscript>
    </section>

    <section class="cache-capacity" aria-labelledby="capacity-heading">
      <div class="cache-section-heading"><div><p class="cache-eyebrow">02 / Explore the tradeoff</p><h2 id="capacity-heading">What does keeping history cost?</h2></div><span class="cache-lane-tag">Size estimate · not a benchmark</span></div>
      <p class="cache-capacity-intro">Keep several checkpoints along one conversation. The proposed cache retains its unique KV rows once, plus private fixed state at each exact boundary. Change the history depth, checkpoint count and budget to see which part grows.</p>
      <div class="cache-capacity-layout">
        <div class="cache-sliders">
          <label for="cache-depth">Latest checkpoint depth<output id="cache-depth-value" for="cache-depth"></output></label><input id="cache-depth" type="range" min="8192" max="151552" step="2048" value="100352" />
          <label for="cache-count">Retained checkpoints<output id="cache-count-value" for="cache-count"></output></label><input id="cache-count" type="range" min="1" max="32" step="1" value="8" />
          <label for="cache-budget">RAM cache budget<output id="cache-budget-value" for="cache-budget"></output></label><input id="cache-budget" type="range" min="1" max="32" step="0.5" value="9" />
          <p id="cache-size-formula" class="cache-method-note"></p>
        </div>
        <div class="cache-capacity-results" aria-live="polite">
          <div class="capacity-row"><div><span>Hybrid · shared KV + fixed state</span><strong id="cache-shared-bytes"></strong></div><div class="capacity-bar"><div id="cache-shared-kv-bar" class="shared-kv-bar"></div><div id="cache-shared-fixed-bar" class="shared-fixed-bar"></div><i class="cache-budget-marker"></i></div><p id="cache-shared-fit"></p></div>
          <div class="capacity-footer"><span><i class="legend-reused"></i>Unique KV <b id="cache-kv-bytes"></b></span><span><i class="legend-fixed"></i>Fixed state <b id="cache-fixed-bytes"></b></span><span>│ Budget</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="cache-method-note">Estimate uses the measured fixed + per-token size model. Checkpoints are 2,048 tokens apart, share one computation history, and have no partial tails. Hybrid totals include reserved spill bytes; session allocations, transfer buffers and allocator overhead are additional. Different conversations and provenance reduce sharing. The record limit is 128.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="cache-reading" aria-labelledby="reading-heading">
      <h2 id="reading-heading">Read the proposal and its evidence</h2>
      <div><a href={`${CACHE_SOURCE}/README.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Proposal overview</span><b>Goals, constraints and research status ↗</b></a><a href={`${CACHE_SOURCE}/hybrid-design.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Hybrid design</span><b>Provenance, spill reservations and disk manifests ↗</b></a><a href={`${CACHE_SOURCE}/experiments.md`} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><span>Evidence</span><b>Measurements and explicitly simulated results ↗</b></a></div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<script>
  import '../scripts/cache-explorer';
</script>
